{
  "endoscopes-never-made-indias-pli-list": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/Olympus_Endoscopes_2_%2815796107708%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\" alt=\"Olympus-branded medical endoscopes on display\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Olympus, the Japanese firm that dominates India's endoscope imports, makes the kind of instrument this piece says PLI-MD never subsidised. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olympus_Endoscopes_2_(15796107708).jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Olympus Endoscopes 2 (15796107708).jpg</a>, Kitmondo Marketplace, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-epr-regime-just-got-teeth-and": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Bebat_battery_mechanical_sorting.jpg/960px-Bebat_battery_mechanical_sorting.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Spent batteries on a mechanical sorting line at a recycling facility\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Mechanical sorting like this is the formal, registered side of battery recycling &#8212; the policy brief's \"black mass\" problem is what happens before batteries ever reach a line like this. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bebat_battery_mechanical_sorting.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bebat battery mechanical sorting.jpg</a>, Bebat organisation, CC BY 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "the-national-beekeeping-honey-mission": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/SAREC_Apiary_-_53078180205.jpg/960px-SAREC_Apiary_-_53078180205.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A beekeeper inspecting a frame full of bees pulled from a hive\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The apiculture the National Beekeeping &amp; Honey Mission subsidised looks like this &#8212; a frame pulled straight from the hive, well upstream of the adulteration this piece tracks. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SAREC_Apiary_-_53078180205.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SAREC Apiary - 53078180205.jpg</a>, Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station, CC BY-SA 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "the-water-bill-nobody-mentions-what": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/TSMC_Fab_18_May_2025.jpg/960px-TSMC_Fab_18_May_2025.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"TSMC's Fab 18 semiconductor fabrication plant complex\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">TSMC's fabs, like this one, are the water-intensive comparison this piece uses to size up what Dholera's 50 MLD treatment plant is actually being asked to handle. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TSMC_Fab_18_May_2025.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TSMC Fab 18 May 2025.jpg</a>, 4300streetcar, CC BY 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indian-railways-98-to-earn-100-business": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Indian_Railways_Locomotive_WDG-4G_of_Roza_Diesel_Loco_Shed_%28ROZD%29_spotted_in_Alipurduar_Dist.%2C_West_Bengal%2C_India_05.jpg/960px-Indian_Railways_Locomotive_WDG-4G_of_Roza_Diesel_Loco_Shed_%28ROZD%29_spotted_in_Alipurduar_Dist.%2C_West_Bengal%2C_India_05.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"An Indian Railways WDG-4G diesel locomotive\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Indian Railways' freight and passenger fleet, run on the &#8377;98-to-earn-&#8377;100 operating ratio this piece examines. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_Railways_Locomotive_WDG-4G_of_Roza_Diesel_Loco_Shed_(ROZD)_spotted_in_Alipurduar_Dist.,_West_Bengal,_India_05.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Indian Railways Locomotive WDG-4G of Roza Diesel Loco Shed (ROZD) spotted in Alipurduar Dist., West Bengal, India 05.jpg</a>, Kingshuk Mondal, CC BY 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "why-bet-on-one-horse-when-you-can-buy": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Horse_Stable_with_trainer.jpg/960px-Horse_Stable_with_trainer.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A horse trainer standing in a stable with several horses\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The piece's title metaphor, literally: betting on one horse versus owning the whole stable, which is what an equal-weighted price-band portfolio actually does. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horse_Stable_with_trainer.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Horse Stable with trainer.jpg</a>, Beersrobert000, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "south-africa-lost-its-gulf-fuel-supply": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Tanker_waiting_to_enter_Durban_harbour.jpg/960px-Tanker_waiting_to_enter_Durban_harbour.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A fuel tanker waiting offshore to enter Durban harbour\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Durban's harbour, the entry point for the fuel imports this piece says South Africa redirected toward the United States rather than India after losing its Gulf supply. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanker_waiting_to_enter_Durban_harbour.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tanker waiting to enter Durban harbour.jpg</a>, Clusteringcoefficient, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "where-indias-captured-carbon-would": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/ONGC_Oil_Platform.jpg/960px-ONGC_Oil_Platform.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"An ONGC offshore oil and gas processing platform at Bombay High\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">ONGC's decades of oil and gas exploration, run from platforms like this one at Bombay High, are the source of the subsurface data this piece says India's CCUS site selection depends on. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ONGC_Oil_Platform.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ONGC Oil Platform.jpg</a>, Nandu Chitnis, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "interest-subvention-built-499-ethanol": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Working_in_the_shadow_of_an_Indian_sugar_mill.jpg/960px-Working_in_the_shadow_of_an_Indian_sugar_mill.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A worker beside an Indian sugar mill\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">India's sugar mills are the base the interest-subvention scheme built 499 ethanol distilleries onto &#8212; the incentive this piece contrasts with the one that produced a single working 2G plant. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Working_in_the_shadow_of_an_Indian_sugar_mill.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Working in the shadow of an Indian sugar mill.jpg</a>, Janoux, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "lemon-cultivation-in-india-steady-trees": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Lemon_from_Assam.jpg/960px-Lemon_from_Assam.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A lemon grown in Assam, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The steady-tree, volatile-price crop this piece tracks, photographed at the point of harvest in Assam. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lemon_from_Assam.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lemon from Assam.jpg</a>, Medhi jyoti, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "tarpaulin-is-genuine-export-win": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Giant_tarpaulin_covering_a_road_under_construction_at_sunrise_with_a_colorful_sky_in_Don_Det_Laos.jpg/960px-Giant_tarpaulin_covering_a_road_under_construction_at_sunrise_with_a_colorful_sky_in_Don_Det_Laos.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A large tarpaulin sheet covering a road under construction\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Tarpaulin doing the kind of large-scale covering work this piece contrasts with the geotextiles India's highway builders still can't source enough of domestically. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giant_tarpaulin_covering_a_road_under_construction_at_sunrise_with_a_colorful_sky_in_Don_Det_Laos.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Giant tarpaulin covering a road under construction at sunrise with a colorful sky in Don Det Laos.jpg</a>, Basile Morin, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "india-exports-worlds-coco-peat-its-own": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Coir_pith_industry.jpg/960px-Coir_pith_industry.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Coir pith (coco peat) being processed at an industrial facility\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Coco peat, the coconut-husk byproduct India exports more of than anywhere else &#8212; and that a scattered few entrepreneurs, not any government programme, are now using to grow the country's own highest-value crop indoors. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coir_pith_industry.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Coir pith industry.jpg</a>, Rprasanth1, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  }
}